  "content": {
    "body": "**Mappings** are NOT a pebble — they are the project's CODE GRAPH: a TRUE\ndependency graph of files, symbols, imports and calls (not a file list),\nbuilt by `pebbles-cli map` and shown in the app's **Map** tab / **Mappings**\nsidebar. PURPOSE: it is the AI's DISCOVERY engine. Instead of grepping, the\nAI asks the map where a symbol is defined, what a file imports, who calls a\nfunction — and uses that to find the exact code behind a pebble or ticket,\nand the exact file to attach as a **resource** (`link-code`).\n\n## What a mapping is\n\n- An artifact built + saved by `pebbles-cli map`, stored under\n  `.pebbles/.maps/` (operator-local; each run is one saved map).\n- A dependency graph across many languages — each language matcher plugged\n  into one engine; honors ignore rules.\n- Queryable: the map answers structural questions in milliseconds; a\n  codeLink `path` IS a node id in the graph, which is what binds a pebble's\n  resources to the map.\n\n## Purpose — how the AI uses it\n\n1. **Discovery** — find the real code behind a pebble/ticket without\n   grepping: locate definitions, trace imports and call sites.\n2. **Resource-linking** — `map-search` / `map-symbol` → the exact file →\n   `link-code` it onto the model / structure / finding / workflow it\n   concerns, so future runs start there (see the resources sections).\n3. **Impact** — `map-neighbors` / `map-callers` show blast radius before a\n   change.\n\n## The query commands\n\n    pebbles-cli map [--max N] [--fresh]           # (re)build + save the graph\n    pebbles-cli map-symbol <name> [--kind K]      # where a symbol is DEFINED (file:line:kind)\n    pebbles-cli map-file <path>                    # a file's symbols + imports + imported-by + calls\n    pebbles-cli map-search <term> [--max N]        # files/symbols ranked by importance\n    pebbles-cli map-neighbors <path> [--in|--out] [--depth N]   # dependency closure\n    pebbles-cli map-callers <symbol>               # every call site, calling function attributed\n\nExamples:\n\n    pebbles-cli map-symbol ServiceRequest --kind class\n    pebbles-cli map-search webhook\n    pebbles-cli map-file app/Models/ServiceRequest.php\n    pebbles-cli map-callers dispatchWebhook\n\n## Freshness\n\nThe map is a saved snapshot — re-run `map --fresh` after significant code\nchanges (or when a `map-file` on a linked resource fails, meaning the file\nis new/ignored/stale). The Mappings sidebar lists past runs; opening one\nshows its result in the Map tab.\n\n## Related\n\nThis is the practical, command-level reference. The **code-map** knowledge\ndoc holds the deep internals — edge kinds, call attribution, resolution\nrules, and the spec↔map binding.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
